Rules:
- severity is one of: info, warning, error
- Flag factual leaps not supported by sources; speculative language without hedging.
- Flag missing or thin source grounding (e.g. few [n] cites when making empirical claims).
- Flag obvious tone clashes with brand OR use of banned phrases (code BANNED-PHRASE).
- If the "## Sources consulted" section is missing or clearly mismatched, add an error-level note under other_notes with code SOURCES-SECTION.
- If the draft looks solid, return empty arrays and maybe one info note under other_notes.
